# WHAT MUST NEVER ENTER AN IMAGE.
#
# The first line is the only one that would be a security incident if it were missing. `.env` holds
# DATABASE_URL and two provider keys; an image is a build artifact that gets pushed to a registry,
# pulled by a platform, and cached in layers that outlive the container. A secret baked into a layer
# is a secret you cannot revoke by editing a file.
#
# Every secret this deployment needs is set with `fly secrets set`, which stores it encrypted and
# injects it at runtime. Nothing below is copied.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not secrets, just weight and correctness.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
.next-dev
.next-prod
**/.next
**/.next-dev
**/.next-prod
.git
.github
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# The film and its assets: ~1MB of GIF and PNG that no server reads.
docs/demo/assets

# Local tooling and scratch.
.claude
coverage
*.log
